hexagon: an index of the readers of each root for the checks of the fused chains

The cost

Each prompt call of the app with a new token count builds a new graph, thus the host matches the fused
chains again: the gate chains of each layer in graph_optimize (ggml_hexagon_gate_keep_inputs) and in
graph_compute (ggml_hexagon_gate_match_all), and the state, conv and norm chains of each gated delta net
layer (ggml_hexagon_match_gdn_fusions). For each candidate chain, ggml_hexagon_gdn_chain_is_private reads
each source of each node of the graph. In the phone stage spf, the host part of a call with a new graph is
15 to 25 ms (the pack 9 to 13 ms, the scheduler allocation 6 to 9 ms). On the build box (hexhost_graphs of
tests/fuzz/hexhost with the 4B Q8_0 in the app configuration, calls of 22 tokens and of 1 token one after
the other, each with a new graph), perf gives 11 % of all samples to ggml_hexagon_gdn_chain_is_private,
which is about 30 % of the host work of such a call.

The change

ggml_hexagon_gdn_readers holds, for each root tensor of one graph, the (node, source slot) pairs whose
source has that root, in node order. The three passes build it one time for each graph and give it to
each chain check. With it, ggml_hexagon_gdn_chain_is_private visits only the sources whose root is the
output or an intermediate of the chain, sorted in node order and source order. These are the only
sources that the full scan acts on, thus the result and the text of a failed condition are the same. A
caller without it (the harness of tests/fuzz/hexhost, for example) keeps the full scan. The passes do not
change the node order while they use it.

The results

The build box, hexhost_graphs of HEAD against the tree with this patch and the three patches before it,
the 4B Q8_0 in the app configuration (op fusion, the fused state step, batch 1024, Q8_0 K and V, flash
attention on):
- The supports_op decisions, the counts of the fused ops, the log, the hazard lists and the verbose text
  of each candidate chain (540 to 971 lines) are the same for the decode, the prefill of 8, 22 and 512
  tokens and the MTP draft step.
- A call with a new graph: 6.46 to 6.89 ms against 5.87 to 5.99 ms. The pack 1.85 to 1.91 ms against
  1.20 ms, the scheduler allocation 1.54 ms against 1.39 ms (the medians of 50 calls, two runs each).
- tests/fuzz/hexhost, run.sh test asan --profile release on the tree with the four patches: 7 suites
  and 0 findings. The graphs of the 2B and the 4B (decode, decode with 4 sequences, prefill, MTP, vision
  576 and 768) give code 0 and the expected counts of the fused conv steps and state chains.
- The phone stage spf2 (the 4B Q8_0 on the v79 NPU, the depth 2300, the draft off), the host part of the
  first call of a size (the wall time minus the wait for the DSP), HEAD against the library with the four
  candidates: 15.6 against 14.5 ms at 1 token, 26.5 against 19.4 ms at 8, 25.7 against 21.9 ms at 22 and
  32.4 against 24.3 ms at 64. The pack 5.06, 12.20, 11.51 and 11.36 ms against 3.68, 8.02, 7.98 and
  6.74 ms.

